[statement]
apk reads the world's names before the installed database's when it
orders removals too: `x` provides `v` at no version, which `ka` and
`kb2304` need, so removing `x` pulls their removals, in the order of apk's
table of names, where the two share a bucket. The world mentions `kb2304`,
so apk reads `ka` last and removes it first. Read in the order of the
installed database alone, `kb2304` would come first (as in
`removals-a-removal-pulls-go-in-the-order-of-apk-s-table-of-names`).

[repository]
P:other
V:1

[installed]
P:x
V:1
p:v

P:ka
V:1
D:v

P:kb2304
V:1
D:v

[world]
!kb2304>5

[request]
other

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
remove ka 1
remove kb2304 1
remove x 1
install other 1
